{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"WAVE 1 - ARM CHARACTERISATION. Compound Engineering is the best FINDER: highest recall (202 TP), highest precision (99%) and materiality (78%), but the worst severity honesty (27% of its own nits marked blocking, including P3 wording fixes) and ZERO BLOCK/PASS discrimination (101 TP on each). superpowers is the best SIGNAL-TO-NOISE: 84 TP from 118 rows, nearly CE's hit rate on under half the volume, and the best severity honesty of any arm at 3%. mini-swe-agent is smallest (77 rows, 98% precision) with zero BLOCK/PASS discrimination, but found 1 of the study's only 2 genuine gaps by going OUTSIDE the plan's stated tree to check a claim against the real tickets branch - no other arm did that. It is also the only arm with a hard dollar cost (.38 avg, .28 worst) and a catastrophic failure mode: at an insufficient step budget it burns the full budget and submits nothing (.75 for zero output before a 260-step retry succeeded). STRUCTURAL FACT: of the 201 issues rebar missed, 156 were found by exactly ONE arm and only 11 by three. The reviewers are near-disjoint - they look at different things rather than being better and worse versions of one instrument. That is the strongest argument in the data for an ensemble."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789000827654007001,"uuid":"09e0be0b-bc6e-4dfa-aa8b-86988663388b"}